WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501
-Standing ovation.
-That's very nice.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.868
Undeserved, but very nice.
-No, no.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:04.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.534
-Do you get a --

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:07.801
Do you get a standing ovation

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.133
when you start "Update"
on Saturday nights?

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.133
-It's in my contract.
-Yeah, okay.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.801
-Why didn't I put it in before?

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.834
-It's been a couple years
since I had you on the show.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:15.834
-I know.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:16.834
-And I'll tell you
what happened.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.167
You got married.
-Yeah.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.501
-Congratulations.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:21.501
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:22.767
-You had a baby.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.901
-I -- We had a baby.
-You had a baby. You guys --

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.167
-I did a little of it.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.334
-Yeah, you did
a little bit of it.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:28.501
Yeah.
Congratulations.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.000
How's married life?
How's the baby?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.834
-It's great.
He's 18 months old.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.167
He's doing great.
He's walking, he's talking.

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.167
His favorite word is "cracker."

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:41.834
Same as Michael Che --
same favorite word.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.934
Same as his uncle.
He got it from his uncle.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.801
-Yeah.
But he's -- he's cute.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.067
-He's great dancing.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.567
He's not really da--
-He's, like, running around?

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.601
-He's walking, but in place.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:54.601
-You brought a photo
of your son.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.267
-We're private, but we...
-So cute.

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.601
-Yeah, this we're --
-Can I show it?

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.400
-Yeah, I mean, it's so cute.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.467
[ Laughter ]
It's like a mix.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.334
You see, it's both of us.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.834
-Yeah, it is. Yeah, yeah.
-There's a little of both of us.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.167
And the dancing is --
the dancing's good.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.334
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.901
-We have Kenya Barris
on the show tonight.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.400
-Oh, yeah.
-And we're talking backstage.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.934
He cast you in
"Coming 2 America."

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.033
-That's right. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.701
-In "Coming to America 2."

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:16.868
The 2 is in the middle,
so it's --

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.200
if you just say it,
it's confusing.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.367
-Oh, that's interesting.
Yeah, you're right.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.868
"Coming 2 America."
-Yeah, so I was --

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:22.200
I believe I was, basically,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.801
the only white character
in the film.

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:25.300
[ Laughter ]
I think it was --

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.300
Louie Anderson came
and reprised his role,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.634
and then it was me.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:31.267
-And you're not gonna believe
it, but I was a villain.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.934
-[ Scoffs ]

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:34.133
-I know.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.300
And weirdly,
I didn't have to audition.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.200
They...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.200
They were just like,
"The part of 'White Villain.'

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.701
I guess we just ask Colin."

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.200
-Yeah.
-"He'll come in and do it."

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.534
And it's really crazy on --
like, when you're doing the role

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.868
because they make me do,
say horrible things.

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:50.934
And then at the --
you know, you're doing it,

00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:52.834
and then when
the director yells "take,"

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:54.334
you have to be like,
"I'm sorry. I'm sorry."

00:01:54.334 --> 00:01:55.834
-Yeah. "I apologize.
That was not me."

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.167
-"I'm just reading
the lines here."

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.868
-Yeah, but then when you
improvise in character

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.434
and it works,
you feel even worse.

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:03.033
-Don't do that.
-You know? Oh, my God.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:06.534
-When you do "Weekend Update,"
are there some times you have,

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.534
the show's off for two weeks
or whatever that --

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.367
and you miss a story,
do you get mad?

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.067
You're like, "Oh, I would have
had a good joke on that one"?

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.501
-I have been following --
I don't know if you guys

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.634
have been following this crazy
murder investigation

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.133
that's happening
in Massachusetts.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:19.133
I know that you guys wanted
to talk about this.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.901
[ Laughter ]
-You knew that?

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.234
-We polled the audience earlier

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:23.434
and they were like,
"Get into that."

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:24.868
-Wait, which one?
-But it was like -- it was --

00:02:24.868 --> 00:02:26.367
it started rolling out on --

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.901
I kept seeing these
headlines on CNN.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.067
And the first headline is like,

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:32.734
you know, "New Year's Day,
wife disappears.

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:33.834
Husband's worried."

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:34.868
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.200
And you realize
"husband worried"

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.367
should just auto-correct
to "husband murdered."

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.033
But they don't...
You can't say that yet.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:41.400
-Yes, exactly.
-So, then --

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.667
Then the next one was like,

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:45.267
"Husband says wife took an Uber
to the airport.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.767
Uber says no."

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:47.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.667
So, like, already,
Uber, of all --

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.167
You know it's bad
when Uber is like,

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:52.767
"This guy's a little sketchy,
I don't know."

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:55.934
And then the next --
-Getting a comment from Uber.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.767
And then the next one is like,

00:02:57.767 --> 00:03:02.067
"Husband says he took his son to
get ice cream, but footage shows

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.400
he went to Home Depot to buy
tarps and a hacksaw."

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.734
[ Laughter ]
-Wait...

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.901
-And you're like, "Whoa,
this really escalated!"

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.234
And then they were like --
then they're like,

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.868
"Alright, we're gonna
bring him in, you know,

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.868
and we're charging him
with misleading investigators."

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:14.534
And his attorney is like,

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:17.133
"What evidence do you even have
against my client?"

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:19.467
They're like, "Well, we found
a bloody knife in the basement."

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.000
-Yeah.
-And the guy's lawyer is like,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.868
"Whoa, you did? Oh, my God."

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.767
[ Laughter ]
"Oh, well, that's not good.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.467
That's, like, classic
bad evidence."

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.300
-Didn't they find --
-And then the Google searches.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.801
-Yes!
-The Google searches.

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.467
There's like hund-- They were
like, "What other evidence?"

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.634
And they had 100 Google searches
and they're literally like,

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.634
"When wife dead,
how long to inherit money?"

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:38.067
-Yes!
-And then, I swear to God,

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.467
one of them was,

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:42.934
"Top 10 ways to dispose of
a body if you really need to."

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:44.200
-Wow.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.601
-He googled a top 10 list.
-He googled it. Yeah.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.100
-He was like,
"Maybe Letterman did it."

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.434
"Maybe he could give me
some ideas on how to do it."

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:54.267
-This week you have Aubrey Plaza
hosting, who is very funny.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.434
-Yeah.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.868
-And she actually said
she interned at "SNL" --

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.367
-Yes.
...for a couple years.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.300
-She interned.
She was in the...

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.434
She worked in our set --
the set design, like, with Leo,

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.200
and it was --
-Did you know her then?

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.701
-Yeah, we were --
we're basically the same age.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.200
We started, like, within a year

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.534
when I started as a writer and
she started as -- in set design.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.300
And then she became a page.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.367
She said she got basically
demoted to being a page

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.033
from having -- running
in the set design,

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.067
working in the set design.

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.901
And so, I've known her
from since then.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:24.167
And I, kind of, in my mind,
thought she had already hosted

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:25.701
because she's so great,
and very I'm excited

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.067
that she's doing it
for the first time.

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:28.634
-She's gonna crush it.
She was great in "White Lotus."

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.934
Yeah.
It's gonna be a great show.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.601
Sam Smith, Aubrey Plaza.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.133
Thank you for being here.
-Oh, my God. Thank you.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.601
-Colin Jost.
Crush it. Break a leg.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:35.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thanks for indulging me...

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:36.767
-Colin Jost, everybody.

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.267
-...my trip down
the investigation.

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:42.200
-"Saturday Night Live" returns
tomorrow on NBC and Peacock

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.701
with host Aubrey Plaza
